{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": [
    "Golden corpus of canonical radio-origin wire events for the MMRelay /",
    "MEDRE interop suite. This file is the SINGLE AUTHORITY that judges BOTH",
    "implementations' Matrix emissions: scenarios/lib/corpus.py validates any",
    "live bot-authored event (from @relay-a, @relay-b, or the medre bot)",
    "against these cases plus the shared contract, using medre's own installed",
    "schema validation (bridge_context normalization + canonical model",
    "construction) as the schema backend.",
    "",
    "A corpus case is an INVARIANT CLASS, not an exact-match fixture: a live",
    "event matches by (event_kind, relation_info, channel) and must satisfy",
    "the shared contract and the case's structural expectations. Each case",
    "also carries a full synthetic wire example; `corpus.py selftest` proves",
    "every example passes the validator and every contract violation class is",
    "actually rejected.",
    "",
    "Wire projection covered here (Matrix message content):",
    "  content.medre.envelope          - provenance envelope (schema v1)",
    "  content.medre.metadata.bridge_context - bounded source claims + relations",
    "",
    "Event-kind mapping (the wire has no 'message.replied' kind): a radio reply",
    "is event_kind message.created carrying relation_info=reply with a",
    "radio-native target_native_ref. The corpus 'replied' cases document that",
    "shape; the 'chain' case documents reply-to-a-reply correlation.",
    "",
    "Adapter ids are OPERATOR-CONFIGURED (mmrelay emits 'mmrelay.meshtastic';",
    "the medre lab rig uses 'radio-a'/'radio-b' for its meshtastic adapters and",
    "'medre' for its matrix adapter). The radio-origin class is therefore pinned",
    "by the numeric channel/packet-id invariants - Matrix-origin channels (room",
    "ids) and native message ids ($event ids) cannot satisfy them.",
    "Meshnet-label isolation (r14/r15 regression class): the meshnet label is",
    "an ATTRIBUTION string. Its canonical home is",
    "bridge_context.source.native_facts.fields.meshnet_label; it may also",
    "appear as bridge_context.source.origin_label (attribution fallback both",
    "implementations emit). It must NEVER occupy a channel-identity field:",
    "envelope.source_channel and source_native_ref.native_channel_id carry",
    "the ORIGIN transport's channel identity only - numeric radio channel ids",
    "('0', '2', ...) for radio origins, the peer's delivery-destination hash",
    "for addressed-transport origins (the source ref's channel may be null",
    "there). Relation-hint TARGET refs follow the TARGET's own transport:",
    "radio-native targets keep numeric channel ids; Matrix-native targets",
    "carry the room id ('!...') plus a $-prefixed Matrix event id.",
    "",
    "Packet ids are unsigned 32-bit integers as decimal strings; ZERO IS VALID",
    "(the zero-target contract: '0' is never dropped as falsy). Live note:",
    "a reply_id=0 tapback is not expressible over the radio wire (proto3",
    "default, proven live 2026-11-10); the zero cases are enforced by the",
    "validator itself and exercised by selftest.",
    "",
    "Reaction emote fallback leading newline (owner ruling 2026-11-12): a",
    "reaction rendered as the m.emote fallback carries EXACTLY ONE intentional",
    "leading newline on its body - mmrelay's radio->Matrix reaction emote",
    "presentation template is the design reference, and two or ZERO leading",
    "newlines is the defect class. Native m.reaction annotations stay bodyless",
    "(no msgtype/body at all); every other body still rejects any leading",
    "newline as the stray fallback-prefix shape."
  ],
  "contract": {
    "envelope_schema_version": 1,
    "event_kinds": ["message.created", "message.reacted"],
    "relation_types": ["reply", "reaction"],
    "numeric_channel_re": "^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$",
    "packet_id_re": "^[0-9]{1,10}$",
    "packet_id_max": 4294967295,
    "fact_key_re": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$",
    "max_bridge_string": 1024,
    "max_facts": 12,
    "max_fact_value": 256,
    "max_relations": 32,
    "radio_text_bytes_max": 227,
    "attribution": {
      "required": ["sender_id"],
      "any_of": ["sender_name", "sender_short_name"]
    }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
